      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2016-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Answer: 36\nA perfect square \\(s\\) divides \\(10^{10}\\) if and only if \\(s=2^{a} \\cdot 5^{b}\\) where \\(a, b \\in\\{0,2,4,6,8,10\\}\\). There are 36 choices, giving 36 different \\(s\\) 's.",
